ne Lean Democratic rating justify only a modest trim toward competitiveness.", "watch": "If Buck's advertising and fundraising begin to register in public polling, or the national midterm environment shifts toward Republicans, the race could tighten to Lean Democratic.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Dina Titus (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Democratic Rep. Dina Titus seeks another term in a Las Vegas-area district that leans Democratic by about two points. She faces Republican challenger Carrie Buck, a strong fundraiser who has raised about $1.9 million, nearly matching the incumbent's total, though Titus holds the cash-on-hand advantage. The two independents on the ballot have raised little and are not significant factors.\n\nProfessional raters mostly place the race at Likely Democratic, with several calling it Safe Democratic and one moving it to Lean Democratic. Betting markets give Titus roughly a 95 percent chance of winning. With no public general-election polling available, the outlook rests on the district's lean, Titus's incumbency, and a midterm environment that currently favors Democrats. Buck's attacks on Titus over gas taxes and energy holdings show Republicans are investing here, but the evidence still points to a clear, if not risk-free, Titus advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 11.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9485, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9231, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9459, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9435, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9451, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-0